rver name)\n29\t  -a alpn         alpn (default function of version)\n30\t  -t file         root trust file\n31\t  -z              Set TLS zero share behavior on client, to force HRR\n32\t  -I length       Length of CNX_ID used by the client, default=8\n33\t  -d ms           Duration of idle timeout in milliseconds (Default 30,000ms)\n34\t  -D              no disk: do not save received files on disk\n35\t  -Q              send a large client hello in order to test post quantum readiness\n36\t  -T file         File storing the session tickets\n37\t  -N file         File storing the new tokens\n38\t  -B number       Set buffer size with SO_SNDBUF SO_RCVBUF\n39\t  -F file         Append performance reports to performance log\n40\t  -V              enable preemptive repeat\n41\t  -U              Version upgrade if server agrees, e.g. -U 6b3343cf\n42\t  -0              Do not use UDP GSO or equivalent\n43\t  -j number       use bdp extension frame(1) or don't (0). Default=0\n44\t  -W bytes        Max value for CWIN. Default=UINT64_MAX\n45\t  -8              Enable SSLKEYLOG\n46\t  -J mode         provider (0), receiver (1) or both (2).\n47\t  -E key config   ECH private key file, config file. Default= no ECH on server.\n48\t  -y public_name  Create an ECH configuration before applying the `ech_s` parameter.\n49\t  -K base64       ECH configuration for the client connection, base64 encoded.\n50\t  -Z bytes        Set the flow control's initial max data.\n51\t  -4 ip[:port]    Preferred address for v4 connections.\n52\t  -6 ipv6[:port]  Preferred address for v6 connections.\n53\t  -h              This help message\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d53c3c63-c627-4b47-883a-4097aa7b6589","uuid":"121e71a2-9f8b-448b-9994-9643ef62a719","timestamp":"2026-05-04T22:48:38.057Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/picoquictest/config_usage_ref.txt","content":"Picoquic options:\n  -c file         cert file\n  -k file  